    {
      "turn": 10,
      "doctor_question": "Have these symptoms continued for more than six months after the schedule changes became the new normal at work?",
      "targeted_symptom": "duration",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, oh yeah, definitely. I mean, the schedule change... that was a while ago now. It's been, what, a year and five months? Something like that. I remember exactly when it started because it was right around the time they rolled out this whole new protocol for the longer rotating shifts, which, let me tell you, threw everyone for a loop. But it wasn't just the shifts, you know? They piled on all this extra documentation we had to do after every single call. Used to be you'd write up a quick report, boom, done, back in service. Now it's like you need a law degree to fill out the paperwork. \n\nAnd then, on top of all that, they decided our house was going to be the one to pilot the new drone program. Which sounds cool, right? Flying drones to scout out structural fires or hazmat situations. But the reality is it's just another massive thing to keep track of—the maintenance logs, the battery cycles, the flight hours. It's endless. So, yeah, ever since all of that hit about a year and a half ago, it's just been a total nightmare trying to keep my head above water. I thought I'd get used to it, you know? Like, you adapt, right? That's what we do. But it hasn't gotten any better. If anything, it's just been this constant, grinding struggle every single day since they made all those changes.",
