    {
      "turn": 11,
      "doctor_question": "Have these symptoms been causing problems in your daily functioning?",
      "targeted_symptom": "functional_impairment",
      "patient_response": "Yeah. Yeah, it really has. I mean, it's gotten to the point where it's not just me being frustrated with myself anymore. It's bleeding into how the guys see me, and in a firehouse, trust is literally everything. If they can't trust you, you're a liability. \n\nLike, just last week, my captain actually pulled me into the office for a formal performance and safety meeting. A safety meeting. Me. I've been doing this for over a decade, and I've always prided myself on being the guy people can rely on when things go sideways. But during the meeting, he brought up all these little things I've been dropping the ball on—forgetting to log the drone battery cycles, missing steps in the new documentation, misplacing the rig keys... just stupid, careless mistakes that I never used to make. He wasn't mean about it, but he was serious. He basically said that if I can't keep track of the details in the station, how can the crew trust me to keep track of the details on a call when lives are on the line? \n\nAnd that just... man, that gutted me. Because he's right. And the worst part is, I've been working my tail off trying to get promoted to lieutenant. I've put in the time, I've taken the classes, I know the job inside and out. But now? I can feel that leadership spot just completely slipping through my fingers. Why would they promote a guy who can't even remember to plug in a radio battery? It's like I'm watching my career stall out right in front of me, and no matter how hard I try to just focus and get it together, I keep messing up the small stuff. So, yeah... it's definitely causing problems. Big ones.",
